From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:02:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Give up on a video VLC cannot read instead of waiting for it
 forever

The video component waited for libvlc_media_parsed_status_done with no
timeout. A file whose parse fails, is skipped or times out (an empty file,
say) never reaches it, so the UI thread waited forever: the screen froze for
as long as the video was on screen, with nobody touching the console once a
system view starts videos on its own.

The parse now has a 2 s timeout, and the wait ends on any final status, with
a hard cap a little past it. Anything but a parsed file is no video: the
snapshot shows (showSnapshotNoVideo too), and the file is remembered by its
path and size, so it is not tried again on every frame or every visit until
it is replaced.
---
